{
  "decline_reason": "",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "There are two separate matters to fix: the classification of the goods and the wording “all goods”; the Manual requires examiners to check both description and classification.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part14/3#1~2",
          "quote": "Examiners must check that goods and services are adequately described and that they are, on the basis of the description supplied, correctly classified."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Regulations require goods and services to be grouped in their appropriate classes, with the appropriate class number nominated for each group.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMR1995/r4.4",
          "quote": "(3) The goods and/or services must be grouped according to the appropriate classes described in Schedule 1. (4) The applicant must nominate the class number that is appropriate to the goods or services in each group."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "legislation"
    },
    {
      "text": "Under the Manual’s practice, misclassified goods can be transferred to the correct class if that class is already included in the application.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part14/4/4/5/1",
          "quote": "Where the specified goods and/or services are not in line with the class number or numbers in which they are filed, it is possible to transfer them to the correct class number if this class also appears on the application."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "If that transfer is not possible, the Manual says the applicant must either delete the misclassified goods or add the necessary class or classes and pay the appropriate additional-class fees.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part14/4/4/5/1",
          "quote": "If misclassified goods or services cannot be transferred in this way, the applicant must either delete them from the application or add an extra class or classes to the application, subject to payment of the appropriate fee for each additional class (fee item 4 of Schedule 9)."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding a class is not permission to widen the specification: the Manual distinguishes allocating goods already claimed to their proper classes from adding goods outside the intended scope.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part14/4/4/8/2~1",
          "quote": "An additional class or classes would therefore widen the specification."
        },
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part14/4/4/8/2~1",
          "quote": "The application could be extended to cover an additional class, because class 5 goods are specified and are intended to be covered by the application. The separation of the goods into the added class would not widen the specification."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "Separately, regulation 4.4(2) prohibits using “all goods” to specify the goods covered by an application.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMR1995/r4.4",
          "quote": "(2) The expression ‘all goods’, ‘all services’, ‘all other goods’, or ‘all other services’ must not be used in an application for registration of a trade mark to specify the goods and/or services in respect of which registration is sought."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "legislation"
    },
    {
      "text": "For a specification containing specific goods plus an unqualified “all goods”, the Manual says the examiner will require deletion of that expression if it remains at examination.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part10/5/5/2/1",
          "quote": "Where an application is made in respect of specific goods and/or services but also includes one of the above non-specific expressions in the specification, that application will be taken as filed but the applicant will be requested, as soon as practicable after filing, to delete the prohibited expression if unqualified. If, at the time of examination, the expression has not been deleted, the examiner will again require the expression to be deleted."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Manual permits additional items within the class claimed to be entered in place of the prohibited wording.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part10/5/5/2/1",
          "quote": "Additional items within the class claimed may be entered in place of the prohibited terms."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "If the description is too vague to classify, the Manual says the examiner should first request further information rather than suggest adding classes at that stage.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part14/4/4/6/2",
          "quote": "If part or all of the specification is vague or unclear to the extent that it cannot be classified, the Examiner should request further information from the applicant. It should not be suggested to the applicant at this stage that they may be able to add a class or classes."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    }
  ],
  "declined": false,
  "concepts_used": [
    "GC-0012",
    "GC-0044",
    "GC-0121",
    "GC-0124"
  ]
}
